# Wave H.f — Neutralize ClubCommerceBadge Denali UX literals

## Problem

Wave F.b moved commerce **policy** to manifest/`isWorkspaceCommerceFrozen`, but `apps/web/src/platform/club-commerce-badge.tsx` still carries Denali product chrome:

| Residue | Why it matters |
| -------- | -------------- |
| `isDenaliWorkspaceType()` alias | Product-named API over a generic freeze helper |
| `data-commerce-denali-frozen` | DOM contract encodes a product id |
| Copy “Denali clubs use offline receipt…” | Hard-coded product marketing in platform Super Admin UI |

Hostile audit still lists “commerce badge literals” after F.b because these strings survived.

## Decision

1. Delete `isDenaliWorkspaceType` (no remaining call sites).
2. Rename attribute to `data-commerce-frozen`.
3. Replace Denali-specific note with product-blind copy: “Frozen commerce workspaces use offline receipt review only.”
4. Keep freeze detection via `isWorkspaceCommerceFrozen` / `shouldShowClubCommerceGatewayUi` (unchanged).
5. Update `platform-club-commerce-badge.spec.ts` assertions to the neutral contract.

## Out of scope

- Webpack `IgnorePlugin` / `ALLOW_*_WEB_PLUGIN` (→ Wave H.g — make gate real; install isolation still later)
- H.e.b custom brand mark component registry
- API `DENALI_FROZEN_COMMERCE_CONFIG` compat alias (Wave F.b intentional)

## Verify

```bash
rg -n 'Denali clubs|data-commerce-denali-frozen|isDenaliWorkspaceType' apps/web
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/platform-club-commerce-badge.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-commerce-badge-neutral.spec.ts
```
